 class="_ac7v x1ty9z65 xzboxd6"><div class="x1lliihq x1n2onr6 xh8yej3 x4gyw5p x14z9mp xhe4ym4 xaudc5v x1j53mea"><a class="x1i10hfl xjbqb8w x1ejq31n x18oe1m7 x1sy0etr xstzfhl x972fbf x10w94by x1qhh985 x14e42zd x9f619 x1ypdohk xt0psk2 x3ct3a4 xdj266r x14z9mp xat24cr x1lziwak xexx8yu xyri2b x18d9i69 x1c1uobl x16tdsg8 x1hl2dhg xggy1nq x1a2a7pz _a6hd" href="https://www.instagram.com/chittinnchattin/reel/DVXTwJSkZL-/" role="link" tabindex="0"><div class="_aagu"><div class="_aagv" style="padding-bottom: 133.333%;"><img alt="this week’s sips of the week feels a little extra enchanting 🫖✨
we’re sipping The Raven from Louisville Tea Co. — a blend that feels like slowing down, grounding in, and letting yourself rest.

black tea for focus and clarity, rooibos for warmth and heart-centered comfort, cacao and chocolate for softness, nourishment, and a little emotional healing. caramel brings sweetness (a reminder to invite ease), while chamomile encourages calm, restoration, and listening to what your body needs.

it’s rich, cozy, and just mysterious enough to feel like a quiet ritual in a cup.
this is the kind of sip that asks you to pause, breathe, and stay awhile 🤍 find us on Spotify, Apple Podcast, and Amazon Music! #ChittinAndChattin
